mate-wayland-session does not run mate-session, so nothing owns
org.gnome.SessionManager on the session bus.  The panel's "Log out" action is a
D-Bus call to that name, so it fails with ServiceUnknown and the button does
nothing.  Start the small provider installed alongside this package; it ends the
session via wayland-logout.

--- a/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
+++ b/session/mate-wayland-components.sh
@@ -23,6 +23,14 @@
 restart_while_running polkit-mate-authentication-agent-1 &
 restart_while_running mate-notification-daemon &
 restart_while_running mate-settings-daemon &
+
+# The panel's "Log out" talks to org.gnome.SessionManager over D-Bus; without
+# mate-session nothing owns that name in this session, so the button does
+# nothing.  This tiny service provides the interface and ends the session via
+# wayland-logout.
+if [ -x /usr/libexec/mate-wayland-session-manager ]; then
+    restart_while_running /usr/libexec/mate-wayland-session-manager &
+fi
 restart_while_running caja -n &
 
 #Programs to start once (if we have them), matching Xorg behavior
